  "patch_sha256": "82690d3d19c0ce7a631709f9e798603f94a65505724198d7674f26f162c8efe4",
  "policy": "Build353 experimental; selective XITRIX Preview 0.10 engine backports (ARM64 SPU/PPU, VM reservations, RSX/Metal, audio recovery, savestate and graphics correctness); Build352 God of War III bounded-memory policy and Build350 lifecycle baseline retained; NeoSwap v1 opt-in host-owned file-backed RSX CPU data allocator, existing JIT/VM/GPU policies unchanged; selective XITRIX v0.10.1 SPU BID continuation, disabled-texture eviction, MoltenVK conditional-rendering fixes; SPU object cache v5 retires old CFG objects; optional NeoSwap client diagnostics ABI 1, main Core ABI 30 unchanged; NeoSwap coherent host-visible Vulkan SYSTEM buffer imports (1-256MiB), strict external-memory/type/alignment checks, deferred GPU resource disposal and allocator fallback; optional NeoSwap guest page relay ABI 1 for guest data shared aliases, host-owned preparation after authenticated creator exit and ordinary file fallback before first published mapping; Build395: measured God of War III opt-in for RSX CPU aligned buffers 64KiB-1MiB via verified donor loans only, fixed metadata budgets, fast pressure gate and original heap fallback; no JIT/VM/GPU/private allocations redirected; Build409: additive NeoSwap client kinds (GPU host-visible imports, owned video-frame mappings) through the unchanged allocator ABI 1, relay host loans selected by the host budget controller; no JIT/VM/GPU/private allocations redirected; Post-410: loading-time SPU guest metadata warmup and telemetry, no ARM64 object persistence; ready-only fast NeoSwap host loans and ordinary guest backing for new gameplay allocations; existing published alias coherence retained; physical device validation pending; Build435 Core delta (10 October 2026): measured per-process allowance in IOSMemoryPressurePolicy (relative moderate stage, adaptive reclaim cooldown), deferred SPU LLVM compilation on a worker pool with legacy-interpreter hand-off, unlocked snapshot precheck before vm::writer_lock on PUTLLC/stcx; no device validation; Build436: the Build435 deferred SPU compilation is switched off (deferred_compile_enabled=false) after God of War III froze about 5 s after boot on the iPhone in 3 of 3 Build435 sessions and another title stopped on SPU STOP 0x0; SPU misses compile inline as in Build434; the measured memory allowance and the writer-lock precheck are kept; no device validation of Build436.; Build436 XITRIX v0.11: five RSX/Vulkan engine commits imported verbatim with their fixtures (framebuffer source selection, Vulkan image-pool race, rendering overhead, divided vertex range, alpha-to-one); no SPU, PPU, JIT, VM or lifecycle change; no device validation of the XITRIX v0.11 import.",
  "schema_version": 2,
